  "summon_profile": null,
  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "invincible global storm: HP-based damage, repeated knock up, Ranged DEF reduction, and rapid true damage strikes",
    "skill1": "Passive: amplifies and keeps ally Haste buffs. Active: channel AoE gusts on enemies from front to back",
    "skill2": "two AoE blade zones on the nearest and farthest enemies, dealing repeated magic damage",
    "skill3": "ATK increase, stacking further with each strike activation",
    "skill4": "ally Haste grants steadfast and damage reduction; strikes build a permanent true damage DoT field with knock up",
    "skill5": "skill hits add true damage, a brief stun, and stacking Vitality reduction"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Marene]] is a backline storm caster built around **Haste**. She amplifies Haste buffs from allies and keeps the bonus after they expire, so she wants **Haste-granting partners**. Enough ally Haste puts her into a **steadfast** state with heavy damage reduction. Her ultimate is invincible and keeps every enemy knocked up while lightning deals **true damage** many times per second. After enough strikes, a **permanent thunderstorm** covers the field with true damage, knock ups, and an execute on low-HP enemies. Her skill hits also stack Vitality reduction. She is weak when **no ally feeds her Haste** and when she is focused before her ultimate fires.",
  "counter_overview": "In PVP, [[Marene]] casts an **invincible** global storm about five seconds in that keeps your whole team knocked up under true damage, and ally-fed **Haste** lets her skills keep shredding even when her ultimate is blocked, so [[Dunlingr]] or [[Lily May]] alone only slow her. Her later **thunderstorm** executes low-HP units unless they are Steadfast or Unaffected: field [[filter:steadfast]] like [[Igor]] or [[Gunnar]], and [[filter:unaffected]] like [[Perseus]] or [[Sylphira]] for the repeated knock ups. The proven answer is **Silence after the storm** from [[Orion]] or [[Contess]], because a silenced Marene deals little damage. Keep that silencer alive through the opener with [[Rolan]]'s max HP and [[Hepler]]'s protection, since her true damage skips shields. Time the Silence between [[Alna]]'s control-immunity cycles when Alna guards her."
}